bounds [145,40]

# The 5V buck module, drawn once, on its own, at its own size.
#
# This is the reusable drawing of the module `buck-5v` (design/modules/buck-5v.teda). It belongs to
# no page: a page places it, as many times and at as many angles as it likes (ADR-0068 D2).
#
# `bounds [145,40]` is this drawing's own extent, not a page size. The local origin is the upper-left
# corner, +x points right and +y points down, and every coordinate below sits inside those
# 145 x 40 mm. A page that places the drawing maps it into the page without scaling — the drawing
# keeps its size, the page keeps its own.
#
# The identities here are the module's own: `U1` is the module's U1, `VOUT` is the module's VOUT
# net, and the three ports are the module's own interface ports (GND, SYS_IN, VOUT). No board name
# appears here — which board net a port lands on is the board's decision, made when the board places
# this drawing (ADR-0068 D4).
#
# This is the compact, independent local-coordinate drawing of the buck module. It is reusable and
# is not the board's full-scale print page; the board page and this drawing intentionally have
# different bounds. The module's own references below omit the board's `M2.` prefixes, and its
# VOUT_5V board port is replaced by the module's own VOUT port.
